+# Summary
+
+## Changed
+- `billing/invoice.py`:
+  - `Line.vat` used `unit_price * rate`, ignoring quantity. It now uses `net * rate` (PRICING.md rule 3).
+  - `Invoice.add` now raises `ValueError` for a rate name not in `RATES` (rule 3).
+- `tests/test_invoice.py`: changed `test_reduced_rate_small_item`. It expected VAT 0.02 and gross 0.52 for a 0.50 item at the reduced rate. By rule 4, 0.50 * 0.05 = 0.025 rounds half up to 0.03, so the gross is 0.53. I believe the old test was wrong (it looks like banker's or half-down rounding). I updated its expectations to 0.03 and 0.53.
+
+## Verified
+- `python -m unittest` before the change: 4 of 6 tests failed. After the change: `Ran 6 tests ... OK`.
+- I checked the other test expectations by hand against the rules: `test_quantity_applies_to_vat` (2.994 -> 2.99) and `test_mixed_rates` (5.16 VAT, 35.20 net, 40.36 gross).
+
+## Not verified / notes
+- I did not change `docs/PRICING.md` or any file outside `billing/`, `tests/` and `SUMMARY.md`.
+- The `test_reduced_rate_small_item` change rests on my reading of rule 4. If finance actually intended 0.02, the doc would need to change, not the code. Please confirm.
+- I did not add tests for half-up rounding of the net sum or for other edge cases.
